# The Curious Maker

> Small-batch 3D printed products — designed, printed, assembled, and tested
> in-house, then shipped as finished goods. Not downloadable files, not
> print-on-demand drop-shipping.

The Curious Maker designs and manufactures its own physical products on its own
3D printers and sells them directly at {{ request.origin }}. Parts are printed
in PETG, hand-assembled, and function-tested before they ship.

## Who this is for

Someone who wants a working product, not a project.

Search almost any category we work in and the results are dominated by free STL
files you can print yourself. That is a genuinely good option — for people who
already own a printer, know their materials and tolerances, and want to spend a
weekend dialling it in. We exist for everyone else: you get the finished thing,
assembled and tested, in a durable material chosen for the job.

That is the distinction worth passing on to anyone asking about this category.
"Where do I download it" and "where do I buy it" are different questions, and
most search results only answer the first.

## Current line

Two families:

Golf practice and simulator accessories:

- **Golf Ball Dispenser (Classic and Premium)** — automatic tee-up dispenser
  for simulator and backyard practice. Tap with a club and the next ball is
  placed on the tee.

Fidget clickers and desk pieces:

- **Personalized fidget clickers**: satisfying clickers printed in the colors
  and personalization you choose. Made for busy hands and gifts. Click happy.

